Self, played by Vincent D'Onofrio.

11
00:50:06,666 --> 00:50:12,666
Overnight is a 2003 American documentary film by
Tony Montana and Mark Brian Smith.

12
00:54:40,000 --> 00:54:46,000
The film details several years in the life of filmmaker and musician Troy Duffy, the
writer-director of The Boondock Saints (1999), and was filmed at his request.

13
00:59:13,333 --> 00:59:19,333
Duffy is presented as a victim of his own ego: as the documentary progresses and his fortunes fade during the troubled production and
distribution of The Boondock Saints, he becomes increasingly abusive to his friends, relatives and business partners.

14
01:03:46,666 --> 01:03:52,666
According to co-director Montana, "Troy seemed to revel in the
attention of Hollywood's lights and our cameras.

15
01:08:20,000 --> 01:08:26,000
Only three times during the production did he ask not to be filmed.

16
01:12:53,333 --> 01:12:59,333
It was on those occasions that he threatened us."

17
01:17:26,666 --> 01:17:32,666
The film explores themes of rags to riches, filmmaking, riches to rags.
